<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Poem</title>
    <style>
        html,
        body {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            min-height: 100%;
            background: #050505;
            color: #f5f5f5;
            font-family: "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
        }

        body {
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            padding: 2rem;
        }

        .poem-shell {
            max-width: 960px;
            width: 100%;
            padding: 3rem 2rem;
            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
            background: rgba(10, 10, 10, 0.85);
            box-shadow: 0 24px 80px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
            backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
        }

        h1 {
            margin: 0 0 1rem;
            font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
            letter-spacing: 0.12em;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            color: #f8f8f8;
            text-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
        }

        .poem {
            margin: 0;
            line-height: 1.8;
            font-size: 1.1rem;
            color: #e8e8e8;
            white-space: pre-wrap;
            word-break: break-word;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>
    <main class="poem-shell">
        <h2>In the End, We are Alone</h2>
        <p class="poem">Everyone has to make it through life on their own.</p>
        <br>

        <p class="poem">Pain sits like a defiant child in a messy bedroom.</p>
        <br>

        <p class="poem">Sometimes the minutes take decades to complete.</p>

        <p class="poem">Second by second. Breathe by breathe.</p>

        <p class="poem">Tic-toc. Tic-toc.</p>
        <br>

        <p class="poem">There is this thing I wanted to tell you about, but I couldn't quite find the words... It was a thought. Well more like feeling. I tried to write it down. I could send it to you, and you would read it slowly. But the words just didn't seem muscular enough to carry the meaning that I wanted to put into them.</p>
        <br>

        <p class="poem">I am going through something. 38 days, 11 hours, and 24 minutes....</p>
        <br>

        <p class="poem">I am always going through something.</p>
        <br>

        <p class="poem">History weighs like a nightmare on the brains of the living.... Marx said that.</p>
        

        <p class="poem">I wonder what he meant.</p>
        <br>

        <p class="poem">So I wrote a few words, I taped them to my chest.</p>

        <p class="poem">I stood up in my bed and tried to recite them from memory.</p>

        <p class="poem">This time I am going to live more openly. This time I am going to be even more vulnerable.</p>
    </main>
</body>

</html>